n't  done that  and you mentioned being a very different  leader i don't think that we've had a  leader that  a 37 year old from the west of scotland  that looks like me from  a muslim heritage that in itself i think  demonstrates a very different scotland  outward-looking scotland international  scotland i should also say that doesn't  say something about me that says  something great about  these people of scotland and and i want  to work with all our diverse communities  to rebuild the country that we love  of course a really big part of the  political landscape in scotland is this  question of  independence um if the snp win a  majority  in the elections that are coming up will  they have a mandate for a second  referendum  look i think the first thing to say in  that is there's a poll out today that  that shows that um  yes is not in the lead so we've heard a  lot about significant polls leading up  to this point  where yes i've been in the lead but i  would go further than that i actually  think it's of course it's for the  scottish people to choose  their own future but actually is it the  right thing to have a referendum  and i think coming through the  collective trauma of covet where we've  been separated from our families and our  loved ones  but we've actually come together like a  country like never before  the idea that we come through this and  go straight into a divisive referendum  campaign i just don't think is the right  thing  to do instead i think it's right that we  focus on rebuilding our country  because what people are worried about  right now is they're worried about their  loved ones staying safe they're worried  when they're going to get a vaccine  they're worried about if and when  they're going to go back to work  they're worried about their child's  education or mental health they're  worried about the planet we're going to  leave  our children our grandchildren they're  worried about the cancelled operations  or the failure to get a cancer diagnosis  because of a pause in the screening  program  these are all massive massive issues and  i would much rather we had political  leadership that focused on those issues  and tried to reunite our country rather  than divide our country again  and on that i actually don't think even  nicola sturgeon would be advocating a  referendum right now  but i think she's more focused on  healing the wounds in our political  party  than she is about healing the wounds in  the country and we will talk about some  of the  wounds as you say in the snp but just to  uh talk for  a bit more about scottish independence  in that referendum i totally understand  that you don't think now is the right  time for a referendum but if the snp win  a majority  in the elections will they have a  mandate for a second referendum i mean  they don't really hide their support for  do they they're called the scottish  national party  yeah they don't hide their support for  it but nicholas sergeant needs to decide  what people are voting on either they're  voting on pandemic record either they're  voting  voting on government record or they're  voting on whether they want to have  an independence referendum look i i  don't want to commentate about what  happens after me  we aren't um spectators we are  participants and i think this is the  challenge for us as a labour party  is if i believe in something i'm going  to argue for it so i don't believe  that independence is the right answer  for scotland coming through this  pandemic  i don't believe coming straight through  this pandemic and going to a referendum  campaign  is the right thing for us to do when our  entire focus should be on saving lives  and livelihoods  and rebuilding our country again and if  i don't believe in something i'm not  going to argue for it  instead what i say to people is let's  have enough  of the politicians trying to present you  with binary choices whether it is yes or  no or leave and remain  and forcing y